# Codebook

## Variables in original dataset 
- Participant - Participant id
- Script - ? (unclear to us what this is)
- Trial - trial id - unique trial items (not what we would call trial, actually item)
- Condition - make, gesture, and no gesture condition (M - make, G - gesture, NG - no gesture)
- Start.time - The start time of the speech
- Transcript - a transcript of what the participant said during trial
- Index.words - Count of diectic references (coded 0, 1, 2, NA). Also uses 'indexical words' in oringinal report.
- Index.speech - Inexicing words used (coded Binary yes, no)
- End.time - End time of trial for participant speech
- Second - duration of trial in seconds
- Word count - number of words spoken in a trial 
- Disfluencies - number of speech disfluencies? (In text written as filled pauses) 
- Timetalking - duration of time speaking as a character vector
- Gesture - Gesture made description - unclear very opaque 
- Iconic - number of iconic gestures
- Beats - number of beats gesture  
- Comments - researchers comments - might just be in excluded trials 
- Letters - number of letters remembered correctly by participant (scored 0-5)
- Location - number of letter locations correctly recalled by participant (scored 0-5)
- Both - number of letter location combinations correctly recalled by particpant (scored 0-5)
- Include - Trial included in analysis (y/n)

## Updated variables used in our scripts
- Participant – unique participant ID (n=49)
- Item – stimulus item identifier (represents grid–pattern pairing). Note: formerly Trial
- Condition – manual behaviour during description task (Gesture, Make, Hands still). Note: renamed original codes (G, M, NG).
- Word_count – dumber of words spoken during the trial
- Time_speaking – duration of speech in seconds
- Filled_pauses – number of speech disfluencies in trial. Note: formally ‘Disfluenices’
- Deictic – deictic speech present (coded 0, 1, 2, NA) Note: formally ‘Index.speech’
- Letters_recalled – number of letters correctly recalled (0–5)
- Locations_recalled – number of letter locations correctly recalled (0–5). Note: formally ‘locations’
- Total_recalled – number of correct letter–location combinations recalled (0–5). Note: formally ‘both’
- Include - include trial in analysis (y/n)
